WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:09.350
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:18.328
Unit fifteen: Writing Task 2: Opinion and Discussion Essays. Today you will write balanced opinion and discussion essays with a clear position.

4
00:00:18.628 --> 00:00:21.164
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.217
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:27.293
Opinion essay.

7
00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:31.873
Opinion essay means an essay that asks if you agree or disagree.

8
00:00:32.483 --> 00:00:34.053
Write an opinion essay.

9
00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.558
Your turn. Say: Opinion essay.

10
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.749
Opinion essay.

11
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:43.868
Discussion essay.

12
00:00:44.883 --> 00:00:48.172
Discussion essay means an essay that discusses two views.

13
00:00:48.783 --> 00:00:51.723
In a discussion essay, discuss both views.

14
00:00:52.317 --> 00:00:55.004
Your turn. Say: Discussion essay.

15
00:00:57.867 --> 00:00:59.471
Discussion essay.

16
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:01.241
To what extent.

17
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.400
To what extent means how much you agree.

18
00:01:05.017 --> 00:01:06.575
To what extent do you agree?

19
00:01:07.183 --> 00:01:09.766
Your turn. Say: To what extent.

20
00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:13.764
To what extent.

21
00:01:14.517 --> 00:01:15.843
In my opinion.

22
00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.418
In my opinion means a phrase to give your view.

23
00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:22.655
In my opinion, uniforms are useful.

24
00:01:23.250 --> 00:01:25.949
Your turn. Say: In my opinion.

25
00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.010
In my opinion.

26
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:31.948
On the one hand.

27
00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:36.308
On the one hand means the first of two contrasting points.

28
00:01:36.917 --> 00:01:38.986
On the one hand, it saves money.

29
00:01:39.583 --> 00:01:42.398
Your turn. Say: On the one hand.

30
00:01:45.233 --> 00:01:46.513
On the one hand.

31
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:48.530
On the other hand.

32
00:01:49.517 --> 00:01:52.468
On the other hand means the second contrasting point.

33
00:01:53.083 --> 00:01:55.222
On the other hand, it limits choice.

34
00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:58.341
Your turn. Say: On the other hand.

35
00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.584
On the other hand.

36
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.339
Concede.

37
00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:08.104
Concede means to accept part of an opposing view.

38
00:02:08.717 --> 00:02:10.890
I concede that some people disagree.

39
00:02:11.483 --> 00:02:13.845
Your turn. Say: Concede.

40
00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.724
Concede.

41
00:02:18.483 --> 00:02:19.775
Nevertheless.

42
00:02:20.783 --> 00:02:23.015
Nevertheless means in spite of that.

43
00:02:23.617 --> 00:02:25.547
Nevertheless, I believe it is right.

44
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:29.174
Your turn. Say: Nevertheless.

45
00:02:32.033 --> 00:02:33.232
Nevertheless.

46
00:02:34.033 --> 00:02:37.870
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:43.166
Visal, what is the difference between an opinion essay and a discussion essay?

48
00:02:44.250 --> 00:02:55.552
An opinion essay asks what you think, for example, to what extent do you agree? A discussion essay asks you to discuss both views and usually to give your own opinion too.

49
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:58.510
How do I show a clear position?

50
00:02:59.617 --> 00:03:11.209
State your position in the introduction and repeat it in the conclusion. Use phrases such as in my opinion or I strongly believe, and keep the same position throughout.

51
00:03:12.317 --> 00:03:13.887
How can I show balance?

52
00:03:14.983 --> 00:03:25.156
You can concede a point from the opposite view, for example, although some people claim it is expensive, I believe the benefits are greater.

53
00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.707
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:32.953
Grammar focus: Strategy: one position, supported throughout.

55
00:03:33.253 --> 00:03:34.393
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:35.083 --> 00:03:39.091
Although some people disagree, I believe that uniforms are beneficial.

57
00:03:39.983 --> 00:03:45.199
On the one hand, uniforms save money; on the other hand, they limit choice.

58
00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:55.148
Identify the essay type, state a clear position in the introduction, and keep it consistent. Use concession to show balance, then explain why your view is stronger.

59
00:03:55.883 --> 00:03:59.940
Be careful! Don't say: I change my position in each paragraph.

60
00:04:01.900 --> 00:04:04.167
Say: I keep one position throughout.

61
00:04:04.467 --> 00:04:05.630
Be consistent.

62
00:04:06.433 --> 00:04:09.341
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:11.727
Uniforms in School.

64
00:04:12.027 --> 00:04:15.268
Some people argue that uniforms limit self-expression.

65
00:04:16.267 --> 00:04:19.741
On the one hand, I concede that students lose some choice.

66
00:04:20.733 --> 00:04:24.184
On the other hand, uniforms save money and reduce pressure.

67
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.792
Nevertheless, I believe the benefits are greater.

68
00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:31.589
In conclusion, schools should keep uniforms.

69
00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:36.806
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.777
An opinion essay asks blank.

71
00:04:40.077 --> 00:04:43.580
A, what you think. B, for a story. C, for a graph.

72
00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:49.330
The answer is A: what you think.

73
00:04:50.483 --> 00:04:52.611
'On the other hand' introduces a blank.

74
00:04:52.911 --> 00:04:57.667
A, spelling. B, contrasting point. C, conclusion only.

75
00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:03.628
The answer is B: contrasting point.

76
00:05:04.783 --> 00:05:06.365
To concede is to blank.

77
00:05:06.665 --> 00:05:12.582
A, refuse everything. B, stop writing. C, accept part of another view.

78
00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:19.526
The answer is C: accept part of another view.

79
00:05:20.683 --> 00:05:22.613
What is the writer's final position?

80
00:05:22.913 --> 00:05:27.484
A, keep uniforms. B, remove uniforms. C, no opinion.

81
00:05:31.033 --> 00:05:33.625
The answer is A: keep uniforms.

82
00:05:34.783 --> 00:05:36.620
Your position should be blank.

83
00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:41.143
A, hidden. B, consistent. C, changed each paragraph.

84
00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.630
The answer is B: consistent.

85
00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:50.834
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:51.683 --> 00:05:54.124
How do you show a clear position in your essay?

87
00:06:02.917 --> 00:06:04.463
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:06:04.763 --> 00:06:21.652
I state my position in the introduction and use it to plan my body paragraphs. I support it with reasons and examples, and I may concede a point from the other side to show balance. In the conclusion, I repeat my position in different words.

89
00:06:21.952 --> 00:06:23.615
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:29.955
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: one position, supported throughout.

91
00:06:30.255 --> 00:06:35.799
Today's value is intellectual honesty. Follow the evidence, even when it is inconvenient.

92
00:06:36.099 --> 00:06:39.053
See you in Unit sixteen. Goodbye!

93
00:06:39.353 --> 00:06:41.831
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

